Description: With Enable 3D off the monitors show the left eye whole
 With the layer's Enable 3D off a monitor declared nothing and showed its
 frames as they are: in a 3D project the frame of two eyes, drawn in the
 monitor's area of one eye's shape, each eye squeezed to half its width, and in
 the clip monitor a 3D clip's packed frame. A program never shows an eye
 squeezed (the stereo contract: "A program never stretches or squeezes an eye;
 KWin scales once, at the output"), and a flat picture of a pair is its left
 eye, as a 2D screen shows it under Stereo KWin. So with Enable 3D off a
 monitor that shows a 3D picture shows its left eye, whole and at its own
 shape, and declares nothing: the picture of Left Eye Only, with the switch
 off. Renders and thumbnails do not change.
 .
 Left Eye Only drew the left half of a frame of two whole views in half of the
 area fitted to the frame. In a 3D project that area already has one eye's
 shape (the project's), so the eye came out squeezed to half its width: the
 monitor is now told that its frames are a 3D project's two eyes and the eye
 fills the area. The settings' labels say what 0 shows now.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Forwarded: not-yet
Last-Update: 2026-11-22
